---
import InteriorLayout from "../layouts/InteriorLayout.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";
---

<InteriorLayout
  title="Terms of Service | V12 Electric"
  description="Read the V12 Electric terms for website use, electrical service inquiries, scheduling links, project information, urgent conditions, and external links."
  image="/images/design-planning.webp"
  imageAlt="Electrical design marked on an architectural plan"
  pageType="article"
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Terms of Service", path: "/terms/" }]}
  showCta={false}
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Terms"
    title="Clear expectations matter."
    description="These terms describe how this website and its inquiry paths are intended to be used."
    image="/images/design-planning.webp"
    alt="Electrical design marked on an architectural plan"
  />

  <article class="legal-page section-pad">
    <p class="legal-meta">Last reviewed: August 5, 2026</p>
    <h2>Website information</h2>
    <p>
      This website shares general information about V12 Electric services and helps prospective
      customers start a conversation. Information on the site is not a quote, diagnosis, permit,
      engineering opinion, or promise that a project can be scheduled.
    </p>

    <h2>Inquiries and scheduling</h2>
    <p>
      Sending an inquiry or selecting a scheduling link does not by itself create a contractor or
      customer relationship, work order, estimate, or service commitment. Scope, availability,
      pricing, permits, utility coordination, and timing must be confirmed directly with V12
      Electric.
    </p>

    <h2>Project responsibilities</h2>
    <p>
      Customers are responsible for providing accurate project information, obtaining property
      access and required owner or association permissions, and identifying conditions that may
      affect the work. Electrical work should be performed and evaluated according to the scope,
      site conditions, applicable codes, and the required authority having jurisdiction.
    </p>

    <h2>Urgent conditions</h2>
    <p>
      This website is not an emergency response service. If there is fire, smoke, exposed
      energized equipment, an immediate safety threat, or another dangerous condition, leave the
      area and call 911 or the appropriate utility or emergency responder first.
    </p>

    <h2>Content and external links</h2>
    <p>
      V12 Electric may update, remove, or correct website content without notice. External booking,
      review, social, map, and other linked services are controlled by their respective providers;
      using one is subject to that provider's terms and privacy policy.
    </p>

    <h2>Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about these terms can be directed to V12 Electric at
      <a href="tel:+17605676593">(760) 567-6593</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</InteriorLayout>
